   422	Then $OP(y, \ell_1, \ldots, \ell_u)$ is solvable whenever the following conditions hold:
   423	\begin{enumerate}
   424	  \item $y = 2x + 3\sum_{\beta=1}^u \ell_\beta -\epsilon$, or
   425	  \item  $y = 2x + 3\sum_{\beta=1}^u \ell_\beta -\epsilon - 2$, provided that $\cG$ satisfies $(\cM)$.
   426	\end{enumerate}
   427	\end{theorem}
