I found a defensible alternative inside Section 2.2: graceful labeling of a “zillion graph” (one path plus several disjoint cycles). I’ll generate a graceful labeling first, erase the labels down to the component lengths, and ask the solver to reconstruct any labeling. The shipped regime will explicitly stay below Theorem 2.4’s constructive bound and require at least three unequal cycles, avoiding the paper’s direct construction and the obvious one-/two-component cases.
