codex
Implemented and verified a graceful-labeling generator based on Section 2.2 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.12713).

The original large-cycle Oberwolfach proposal was discarded because the paper gives an explicit construction for that regime. The shipped family instead uses short-path, multi-cycle zillion graphs outside Theorem 2.4’s constructive bound.

Deliverables:

- [gen_2306_12713.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.12713/gen_2306_12713.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.12713/selftest_report.json)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.12713/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.12713/README.md)
- [.meta.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2306.12713/.meta.json)

Key results:

- All G1–G8 gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- All three adversarial attacks failed across eight instances.
- Canonical-key audit: 20/20 unrelated keys distinct.
- Additional sweep: 200/200 planted witnesses verified.
- Oracle verdict: `hardened` at `easy`, with three distinct vendors returning parseable but invalid witnesses.
- Shipping parameters: `n=64`, at least three cycles with three distinct lengths.
